{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793376520,"nonce":"pU47bCzm6AnQcLIEOoVJvqjhu28=","title":"Cranelift: a call to a function missing from function_map compiles to the constant 0","message":"cranelift_backend.rs, HirCallable::Function translation: when the callee has no entry in function_map, the backend logs `Function {:?} not in function_map` at warn level and binds the call's result to `iconst 0`, dropping the call. compile_module removes a function from function_map when its body fails to compile (\"Remove from function_map to prevent later lookup failures\"), so every caller compiled after it silently loses the call: a side effect vanishes and a result reads as 0 (null).\n\nFound through portable code (09dc35a): a portable compile that refused zl_arr_shared and zb_list_box_any compiled zl_arr_box to return 0 on both paths, and zl_rawgeti later read through the null array. Portable mode now keeps the declaration and makes the missing callee an error; the JIT path still has the fallback.\n\nThe call should be an error (the caller then stays interpreted or is declined), or the failed function should keep its declaration and be reached through its cell or a stub. Check what loses compiled coverage when it errors before changing it.","files":null}]}